{
  "title": "T.R.I.S.T.A.N. local model benchmark, round two (issue #90)",
  "machine": "Apple M4 Pro, 48 GB memory",
  "ollama_version": "0.40.14",
  "dates": {
    "first_pass_7_tasks": "2026-11-08",
    "rerun_9_tasks_and_cloud": "2026-11-09"
  },
  "method": {
    "script": "scripts/bench-ollama.py",
    "runs_per_task": 3,
    "local_options": {
      "temperature": 0,
      "seed": 1,
      "num_predict": 2048
    },
    "cloud_options": "no temperature or seed sent (reasoning models); max_completion_tokens 4096",
    "tasks_first_pass": [
      "tool_read",
      "tool_edit",
      "tool_run",
      "no_tool",
      "spoken_line",
      "code",
      "context"
    ],
    "tasks_rerun_adds": [
      "multi_step",
      "denied"
    ],
    "scoring": "every pass or fail is a rule in the script; no person read the answers",
    "notes": [
      "The 3 runs are near-identical repeats at temperature 0 with a fixed seed, so 3/3 shows a steady answer, not three independent samples.",
      "tokens_per_second is the median over all generated answers; for the cloud models it is the whole call including the network, so it is not comparable with the local figures.",
      "loaded_gb is what Ollama reported after the long-context task (about 10,000 tokens of context), so it includes working memory.",
      "cold_start: the model was unloaded, then asked 'Say ok.' once. load_seconds is the load, prompt_seconds the time to read the prompt (the first-token wait).",
      "Times for warm runs are not published: Ollama's prompt cache made them close to zero.",
      "The seven original tasks use an edit_file tool the app does not have; multi_step and denied use the app's real four tools, system prompt and denial message."
    ]
  },
